            {
              "type": "Progress Notes",
              "title": "New Patient Visit",
              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2022-09-13T10:30",
              "body": "21 y/o F here to establish. Previously seen at a pediatric practice in town through high school and college health since; aged out and her parents wanted her somewhere she could reach by text. No complaints today.\n\nPMH: none. No hospitalizations. PSH: none.\nMeds: none. No OTC or supplements.\nAllergies: NKDA.\nFH: father with HTN. Mother with hypothyroidism. Maternal grandmother had breast cancer at 65. No early heart disease, no colon cancer known.\nSH: full-time at the university, works part time in retail on weekends. Lives in an apartment off campus with a roommate. Never smoked, never vaped. Alcohol a couple of drinks a month, social. No drugs. Sexually active; declines to go into more detail today, agreeable to routine STI screening.\nGyn: menarche around 12, cycles regular. Has not had a Pap yet.\n\nROS: negative in full.\n\nExam: well, pleasant. HEENT clear, TMs normal. Neck supple, thyroid not enlarged. Heart RRR, no murmur. Lungs clear. Abdomen soft, NT, no masses. Skin clear. Neuro grossly normal. Mood bright.\nPHQ-2 0, GAD-7 2, AUDIT-C 2.\n\nA/P: healthy young adult, establishing care.\n- Baseline lipids, CBC, CMP.\n- One-time HIV and hepatitis C screens; urine GC/CT given age.\n- Immunizations: will pull the pediatric record. Flu shot next month when clinic stock arrives.\n- First Pap due; she would rather do it next visit. Fine, we will plan for next fall.\n- Gave her the practice cell number. Return in a year."
            }
